WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.812
Before creating a view, make four decisions.

00:00:02.812 --> 00:00:06.057
Choose a meaningful name. Define the row grain.

00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:11.072
Choose the columns intentionally. Then write the SELECT that implements that interface.

00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:15.067
Starting with the contract makes the SQL easier to evaluate.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:19.737
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:19.737 --> 00:00:25.707
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:27.962
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:34.117
In a real setting such as a governance project limiting which columns different users can access,

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:40.332
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:41.827
before discussing syntax.

00:00:41.827 --> 00:00:47.920
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
